David Tong, University of Cambridge. [Author's course page](https://davidtong.org/teaching/classical-dynamics/) · [Complete 139-page PDF](https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/classical-dynamics/clas.pdf).

The inspected cover dates the notes to Michaelmas 2004 and 2005. The author describes a second course for final-year undergraduates. Four chapters develop Newtonian, Lagrangian, rigid-body and Hamiltonian mechanics; four problem sheets accompany them. Use printed section and page numbers, which differ from PDF page positions. The expanded commercial textbook is a separate publication.

The course page, cover, contents and selected sections on constraints, small oscillations and rigid-body rotation were inspected on 30 October 2026. Begin with the earlier engineering dynamics work; use these notes for sustained derivation and advanced studies. Complete chapters and their problems deepen the mathematical account beyond a formula catalogue.

The author provides the notes for free reading. No general adaptation licence was established from the inspected page or PDF. Link the authorized files, preserve attribution and inspect any component notices before redistribution. The former Cambridge-hosted course URL redirects to this author site. No PDF is bundled here.

