**Seventh physics-core inspection — 1 November 2026:** the current author-hosted course page and actual Michaelmas 2004/2005 PDF were inspected. Selected printed pages 50–54, sections 3.2–3.3, supply kinetic energy, the inertia tensor, its quadratic form, parallel-axis reasoning, L=Iω and the center-of-mass decomposition. The body-frame Euler-equation passage was also inspected as a limit on scalar fixed-axis dynamics. The common lesson explicitly retains the zero-inertia direction for ideal collinear mass, so nonnegativity is not silently strengthened to strict positivity. Complete the original progressive mechanics assignment as its prerequisites develop; no complete chapter/problem-sheet audit or solved gyroscope study is claimed. The author provides free reading; a general adaptation licence remains unestablished. All source media remain external.

